# The current head cannot express a four-deep pairing in the coverage
# reserve: re-open the enumeration front on today's tree

## Goal

Make the approximate mode enumerate `hits justice dupe hid came` for
`It's just a stupid game` as a result of general traversal behaviour, never a
phrase-specific hard-code.

This is a **re-opening on the current head** of the enumeration territory
[w-2f7a10](w-2f7a10.md) owns, prompted by two facts that are new since that
item's last note.

## Why this is a new item

1. **[w-d4a90b](w-d4a90b.md) localised the loss to enumeration, not the
   objective.** On `f5b9eaa` the phrase is absent from the **entire** pool
   (missing from all 17 827 candidates at `--top 50`, all 13 498 at CLI default
   `top_n` 10), so it has **no rank**. It is nevertheless admissible under the
   shipped budgets (per-word costs `0.2 / 0.0 / 0.15 / 0.3695 / 0.4`, total
   `1.11951981` <= `1.5`, exactly one complete lattice alignment) and scoreable
   at `0.79990129077367222`, i.e. `0.09785131568084526` below the worst visible
   proposal at `--top 50`. So it is dropped **before the pool is formed**: no
   score, admission, share-cap or cutoff change can surface it.

2. **The reviewed reserve-shape fix that raises the deep cap is still not
   integrated, and the constant on the current head still forbids the shape.**
   `src/lib.rs:212` on `post-milestone-acceptance` is
   `const EMIT_PROFILE_MAX_DEEP: usize = 3;` while `coverage_tuples`
   (`src/lib.rs:384`) walks slot subsets breadth-before-depth and emits
   subsets of size `1..=max_deep`. The change that raised the cap to 4 and made
   each member of a shape class draw its own coordinate exists, was reviewed
   for generality, and was deliberately **held** pending a breadth measurement
   (commits `a58a49b` and the continuity clause `3b14482` on
   `madgab-pairing-2f7a10`, report `REPORT-2f7a11.md`). The **sweep** half of
   that work *was* integrated (`e123dbb`, per-member coprime sweep rates at
   `sweep_index`, `src/lib.rs:302`); the **depth-cap** half was not.

So the concrete question this front owns is narrow and answerable: **on the
current head, is `EMIT_PROFILE_MAX_DEEP = 3` the binding reason the requested
wording is never offered as a tuple, and is raising it justified by its own
arithmetic rather than by the phrase?** The independent arm
[w-5d2a91](w-5d2a91.md) re-derives the depth measurement so the implementer is
not the only source of it.

## Hypotheses, in order

1. **Depth cap.** Count how many of the requested wording's coordinates are
   simultaneously off the traversal's best index in its own slot's ranked list
   on **this** head (the older figures were 7 / 0 / 13 / 99 / 11 per slot, i.e.
   four deep, on a three-axis-old tree). If it is four, the reserve on this head
   cannot express the tuple at any phase, and the 17:47Z pass already measured
   that raising the cap 3 -> 5 with nothing else changed moved canonical
   members 47 -> 47, because the *order* was the gate then. Re-measure that
   arithmetic: the order has since changed (`profile_tuple`, interleaved
   depths, `COVERAGE_SLOT_ROTATION`), so the old refutation may not hold.
2. **Per-structure retention.** The structure `[3, 10, 13, 15, 19]` is
   populated; check whether `SEGMENTATION_KEEP` or the pool's per-structure cap
   is what bounds it, and whether an under-represented structure is crowded
   out by structures with more members.
3. **The cost bound.** `build` compares each tuple's total substitution cost
   against `total_budget` additively. The requested tuple costs
   `1.11951981` of `1.5`, so this is expected to be refuted — measure it rather
   than assume it.

A refutation of hypothesis 1 is an acceptable and useful result; record it and
route on the next gate.

## Scope and collision boundary

This front owns the traversal's **tuple space** on the current head:
`coverage_tuples`, `profile_tuple`, `sweep_index`, `sweep_rate`,
`EMIT_PROFILE_MAX_DEEP`, `EMIT_PROFILE_RESERVE`,
`LEXICAL_COMBINATIONS_PER_SEGMENTATION`, the per-slot candidate lists, the
emission-budget accounting in `build`, and per-structure retention in the pool.
It may read `axes::*` and `select_diverse` to diagnose but must not change them.

Forbidden: sweeping or re-tuning `axes::*` weights or any `boundary_novelty`
form ([w-3f9c02](w-3f9c02.md)), `src/adjacency.rs` and `ADJACENCY_*`, changing
`select_diverse`'s admission order or the share cap / `STRUCTURE_FLOOR`
([w-8a1d47](w-8a1d47.md)), relaxing or re-baselining **either** acceptance
test, and any phrase-specific case in `src/` or `tests/`. `approximate_output_is_locked`
may be re-baselined only with a record of which structures moved, and only as a
consequence of this item's own change. Do not merge any `scratch/*` branch
(including `scratch/2f7a10-base`, `scratch/2f7a10-verify`,
`scratch/2f7a10-tip-verify`, `scratch/9f1c05-aggform`) and do not touch another
front's worktree.

## Completion criteria

1. **Diagnosis first, by line.** On the current head, the function, line and
   rejecting quantity where the requested tuple is never offered; the count of
   tuples `coverage_tuples` does offer for that structure across a run, and the
   count it would need. Measured on the **default** approximate path with a
   release build.
2. **A landed, general fix** if a fix is warranted, argued from the mechanism
   and never from either phrase: no special case for any word, substring or
   word sequence of either acceptance example, in `src/` or `tests/`. If the
   depth cap is the gate, say **what it now bounds**, with arithmetic, and
   derive any extra spend from the emission/pop budget the search already
   respects rather than raising an unrelated constant. If the held
   `a58a49b` / `3b14482` change is the right one, re-measure its breadth cost
   on the current head and say whether it is restored or only explained.
3. **A regression test** expressing the general property — a *pairing* of deep
   alternatives in different slots is reachable in the approximate pool, not
   merely each alternative alone — naming neither acceptance phrase, and
   **shown red on the base it claims to fix**.
4. **Membership on the default release path**: the count of pool candidates
   containing the requested wording goes from 0 to non-zero, with the same
   count reported for six real targets that contain neither acceptance example,
   so the change is shown not to be specific to one input.
5. `approximate_finds_recognize_speech_resegmentation` and
   `approximate_pool_reaches_alternatives_past_the_opening_slot_width` stay
   green — they are guards, not targets. Re-measure `recognize speech` after
   any pool-changing fix rather than only before it.
6. `cargo test --release --lib`, `--test corpus_integration`,
   `--test exact_determinism`, `--test approx_determinism` and
   `--test no_phrase_hard_coding` reported. `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy` and
   doctests do not exist on this host ([../../environment-notes.md](../../environment-notes.md));
   do not claim them.
7. Wall clock on `--approximate --top 50` not regressed, measured **interleaved
   against the base in the same session** — [w-7b2d40](w-7b2d40.md)'s
   1.77-2.51 s column is host noise and [w-d4a90b](w-d4a90b.md)'s ~2.2-2.5 s
   is a third session.

