## Front report: agent `1c3e77`, resumed on `madgab-enum-depth4` at `03fdf52`

Branch `madgab-enum-depth4`, one commit: **`784deaa`**. Nothing is
integrated by this front; `post-milestone-acceptance` and `main` are
untouched.

### Objective state: NOT met, and shown not reachable by enumeration

**`approximate_finds_classic_madgab_resegmentation` does not pass on this
branch.** Its assertion is unmodified. It was red on `03fdf52` and is red
on `784deaa` for the same reason: the wording is never enumerated.

Reported separately, as the coordinator asked:

* **ENUMERATED — no.** `hits justice dupe hid came` is still absent from
  the pool on the default release path, before and after `784deaa`.
* **RANKED — no, and unreachable by this class of fix.** On the base, with
  the wording *force-emitted* into the pool by a probe (not landed), the
  real final scorer gave it **`0.799901`** and it sat at **rank 9 997 of
  17 826** pool candidates, with 48 candidates of its own structure
  `[3, 10, 13, 15]` and that structure's best at rank 3 376. The visible
  cutoff for `--top 50` is `0.898`. `select_diverse` fills its 50 slots
  from the head of the score order, so a candidate at rank 9 997 cannot be
  shown whatever the search enumerates. **The test is therefore a
  visibility assertion, not a pool-membership assertion**, and no change
  to search, segmentation, index-space construction, retention, budget or
  emission can turn it green. Unblocking it requires changing something
  this front is forbidden to touch — see "Unblocking condition" below.

### What the log established before the change (do not re-measure)

On the head `03fdf52`, release, default path, target
`It's just a stupid game` (IPA length 19):

* the target's structure is spans `(0,3) (3,10) (10,13) (13,15) (15,19)`,
  retained at segmentation rank 151 of 256, per-slot candidate-list widths
  `[160, 7, 160, 160, 93]`;
* ranks of the requested words in each slot's contribution-sorted list are
  **22 / 0 / 64 / 85 / 7**, costs `0.2 / 0.0 / 0.15 / 0.3695 / 0.4`,
  total `1.1195` of a `1.5` budget — so four coordinates are off the
  corner *simultaneously*, and one of them (7) is below
  `LEXICAL_BRANCH_STAGE_0`, which is the width the coverage reserve's
  sweep floor is tied to;
* the per-slot **budget-derived depth equals the list width in every one
  of the 256 retained segmentations** (slack 0.5–1.4 of a 1.5 budget), so
  the affordability model the brief names cannot truncate anything at the
  shipped budgets. That is why the landed half of this front is inert at
  default budgets and is documented as such;
* opening every slot at the full `160` and raising the pop limit to
  200 000 (measured on the base, not landed) does **not** put the wording
  in the pool: with a best-first walk on the final score, the count of
  better-bound tuples in front of a four-deep point in a 160·160·160·93
  product is astronomically larger than any per-segmentation budget. This
  is the "no score-monotone enumeration reaches it" arithmetic the
  coordinator has accepted.

### What landed on `784deaa`, and why it is general

Two changes, both in the lexical phase's affordability model, both derived
from budgets the search already respects. Neither mentions any word,
clue or substring of either acceptance example.

1. **Per-slot affordability, read one candidate at a time**
   (`slot_is_affordable`, `src/lib.rs`). A candidate is pushed only if
   `committed(prefix) + min(later slots) + cost(candidate) <= total_budget`
   — exactly the tail of the additive sum `build` already applied at the
   leaf, decided where it can still save work. Nothing `build` would have
   kept is rejected. Measured discarded fraction at the shipped budgets:
   **669 of 15 875** built wordings on one target, **87 of 13 640** on
   another, so it is nearly inert by default and binds when a caller
   tightens `total_budget`. Stated in the code as a bound, not claimed as
   a win.

2. **The traversal's opening width, derived rather than uniform**
   (`affordable_opening_width`, `src/lib.rs`). A best-first walk over `d`
   slots reaches its first wording only after `1 + w + ... + w^(d-1)` pops.
   At `w = 10` and a 4 000-pop limit: `d = 4` needs 1 111 and reaches its
   first wording; `d = 5` needs 11 111 and does not. So a segmentation
   past the crossover was not *poorly* funded, it was funded with a budget
   that cannot be spent at all. Measured on the default release path,
   **27 of 256** retained segmentations emitted no wording whatsoever on
   `It's just a stupid game`, **109** on `a whole lot of trouble`, **84**
   on `the cat sat on the mat`, each after spending its full 4 000 pops
   out of the *global* pop budget, paid for by the segmentations that do
   emit. The new function takes the largest `w` whose series fits the pop
   limit, capped by `LEXICAL_BRANCH_STAGE_0`, so below the crossover
   nothing changes and `next_branch_stage`'s widening ladder is untouched.

**Purpose of each bound, before and after.**

| bound | before | after |
| --- | --- | --- |
| per-slot candidate width | whole contribution list; cost budget checked only at the leaf | candidates the total budget cannot pay for are never pushed; the index space is the affordable one |
| traversal opening width | `LEXICAL_BRANCH_STAGE_0`, uniform in the slot count, i.e. a function of nothing | largest `w` with `1 + w + ... + w^(d-1) <= LEXICAL_HEAP_POP_LIMIT`, capped by `LEXICAL_BRANCH_STAGE_0` and by the widest list |
| `LEXICAL_HEAP_POP_LIMIT` | 4 000 per segmentation; unpayable past ~4 slots | unchanged; now actually payable at every slot count, because the width is derived from it |
| `EMIT_PROFILE_RESERVE` / `coverage_tuples` / `sweep_index` / `EMIT_PROFILE_MAX_DEEP` | 16 / breadth-before-depth / floor `LEXICAL_BRANCH_STAGE_0` / 3 | **unchanged — not this front's territory** (9c4d21 owns the reserve) |
| `SEGMENTATION_KEEP` | 256 retained alignments | unchanged |

**Measured effect, base `03fdf52` → `784deaa`, default release path:**

* pool size (`generate_with_pool`, `top_n = 20 000`): 19 511 → 20 500,
  17 277 → 19 542, 17 919 → 22 981, 18 358 → 21 565, 16 525 → 21 294,
  14 880 → 15 485, 11 048 → 11 333.
* search wall clock, interleaved in one session, three runs each:
  1 840 → 1 176 ms, 1 716 → 1 128 ms, 2 205 → 1 186 ms.
* visible `--top 50` quality and the share/diversity profile are
  unchanged (worst visible 0.898 → 0.897, 0.882 → 0.887, identical
  elsewhere).
* **The trade, stated rather than hidden:** the number of *distinct* deep
  resegmentations in the pool falls (47 → 32 of six slots or more on
  `she sells sea shells`; 336 → 310 structures on
  `It's just a stupid game`), because the same pops now go to fewer,
  actually-funded structures. Distinct words drawn on is flat to slightly
  down (1 490 → 1 469 on that target).

